## Page Template

Every wiki page should follow this structure. The frontmatter block is required on every concept, framework, and entity page.

```markdown
---
confidence: [value from confidence taxonomy above]
source-date: YYYY-MM-DD
tags: [domain-slug, domain-slug]
---

# [Page Title]

**Domain(s):** [all that apply]
**Folder:** [which wiki subfolder this lives in]
**Sources:** [wiki-links to source summary pages that contributed to this]

## Overview
[Lead with the actionable claim — what this concept IS or DOES. Source voice if VOICE_PRESERVATION=yes.]

## [Content sections — varies by page type]

## Conflict
[Optional — use when the source diverges from mainstream or when two sources disagree. Structure:]

**Mainstream view:** [paraphrase + source]
**[Source name]'s view:** [paraphrase + [[wiki-link]]]
**Why it matters:** [practical consequence of the disagreement]

## {{VOICE_SECTION_HEADER}}
[Exact phrases, analogies, one-liners from the source — 5-15 quotes minimum. Each ends with a source anchor: — [Module 3, Book Title | Author, Year | Platform: Title]]

## Cross-Domain Connections
> **Cross-domain:** [How this connects to the owner's specific situation — actual numbers, portfolio, business — not abstract principles]

## Related Pages
- [[link]] — [why it's related, one sentence]

## Gaps
- GAP: [anything missing that should be here]
```

