## Source Page Template

Every `wiki/sources/<slug>.md` page must follow this exact structure:

```markdown
# Source: [Full Title]

> **Historical context:** [Why this was written and what it responded to. Required for polemical, crisis-era, or time-sensitive documents.]

- **Type:** [memo | letter | transcript | book chapter | course module | etc.]
- **Content Date:** [Publication date of the original — NOT when you processed it]
- **Domain(s):** [list]
- **File path:** `raw/<relative/path>`

## Abstract / Key Question
[3 sentences: what the document is + what question it answers + why it was written]

## Key Findings
1. **[Bold header]** [Substantive paragraph with embedded verbatim quotes]
...
10. **[Bold header]** [...]

## {{VOICE_SECTION_HEADER}}
[10–15 verbatim quotes, each ending with: — [Source anchor]]

## Cross-Domain Connections
> **Cross-domain:** [Personalized to owner's specific situation]

## Related Pages
- [[wiki-slug]] — [why related]

## Pages Created/Updated: (pending Pass B)

## Candidate New Pages (Pass B)
- `wiki/<folder>/<slug>.md` — [description] — Supporting quote: "[verbatim]"
- `wiki/<folder>/<slug>.md` — [description] — Supporting quote: "[verbatim]"
- `wiki/<folder>/<slug>.md` — [description] — Supporting quote: "[verbatim]"

## Gaps
- GAP: [specific gaps — unread sections, missing data, unverified claims]
```

